{"nodes": [{"id": "vault_adr_0160_glue_homes_service_in_its_engine_decision", "label": "ADR 0160: GLUE Home's service in its engine: the hidden page removed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "rationale": "Moved GLUE Home's service from a hidden WebView into the Rust engine to save ~40MB private memory and keep behavior unified in one language. The final batch (E5) of the plan to port service work from TypeScript to Rust."}, {"id": "service_rs_module_concept", "label": "crates/glue-engine/src/service.rs: service implementation", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "rationale": "Implements GLUE Home's service: status_json, events (last 30), served (what devices asked), receiving (songs), service_start (tokens, GLUE folder, songs, music folders, timers), control (Start/Stop/Restart), config_changed."}, {"id": "verify_rs_module_concept", "label": "crates/glue-engine/src/verify.rs: native check", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "rationale": "Moved from GLUE Home's analysis.rs. Compares samples and drives the loop for native engine verification."}, {"id": "one_engine_design_concept", "label": "GLUE Home keeps one engine for its whole run", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "rationale": "GLUE folder changes in place (Engine::set_glue) with stores let go and songs re-scanned, instead of creating new engine. Allows service, room, sessions to carry on across folder changes."}, {"id": "e2e_test_stand_in_architecture_concept", "label": "E2E test stand-in architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "rationale": "Test engine starts service with GLUE Home's initial settings, receives later settings as config_changed. GLUE Home's background (room socket, connections) runs in __e2e/home.html (__e2e/home.html, e2e/home-public/, never shipped), separate from settings window, matching Rust architecture."}], "edges": [{"source": "vault_adr_0160_glue_homes_service_in_its_engine_decision", "target": "vault_adr_0044_glue_home_tauri_tray_app_decision", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_adr_0160_glue_homes_service_in_its_engine_decision", "target": "vault_adr_0152_the_library_store_in_rust_decision", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_adr_0160_glue_homes_service_in_its_engine_decision", "target": "vault_adr_0153_the_library_engine_in_rust_decision", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_adr_0160_glue_homes_service_in_its_engine_decision", "target": "vault_adr_0154_the_analysis_queue_in_rust_decision", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_adr_0160_glue_homes_service_in_its_engine_decision", "target": "vault_adr_0155_the_shared_sync_in_rust_decision", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_adr_0160_glue_homes_service_in_its_engine_decision", "target": "vault_adr_0156_the_answers_to_other_devices_in_rust_decision", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "vault/adr/0160-glue-homes-service-in-its-engine.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_adr_0160_glue_homes_service_in_its_engine_decision", "target": "vault_adr_0157_one_analys